This pull request updates how the RDS Proxy application user is configured for Aurora PostgreSQL clusters. The main change is to switch from using a Secrets Manager secret for the application user to using an IAM-only database user (rds_iam). This simplifies configuration and removes the need to manage a separate secret for the application user. The changes also update variable and output names to reflect this new approach.

RDS Proxy Application User Refactor

Replaced the rds_proxy_application_secret_arn variable with rds_proxy_application_username throughout the configuration, making the application user IAM-only and removing the need for a Secrets Manager secret. [1] [2] [3]
Updated the RDS Proxy module logic to use the new rds_proxy_application_username variable, and removed all references to the previous secret-based authentication. This includes simplifying IAM policy grants and removing the dynamic auth block for the application user. [1] [2] [3] [4]
Updated environment variable files (dev.tfvars, prod.tfvars) to provide the new rds_proxy_application_username value instead of a secret ARN. [1] [2]
Outputs and Documentation

Added a new output rds_proxy_application_username to both the main and module outputs, making the IAM-only application user visible to consumers. [1] [2]
Improved documentation and comments to clarify the new IAM-only authentication flow for the RDS Proxy application user.
These changes make the RDS Proxy application user configuration more secure and easier to manage by leveraging IAM authentication without requiring additional secrets.

